   "evidence": "grep: `code/EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/LightFront.lean:321-326` (`def relativeTransverse (k P : Vector 3) : E\u00b2 := transversePart k - (plusComponent k / plusComponent P) \u2022 transversePart P`) versus the new `LightCone.lean:94` definition with `xiLC L K = L.plus (deltaLost K) / L.plus K.p` (LightCone.lean:47-48) \u2014 identical formula. `grep -rn relativeTransverse EpsilonEridani` returns only LightFront.lean, so there is no existing bridge.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics/LightCone.lean",
   "fix": "Define the general version once in its canonical home, `Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/LightConeBasis.lean` \u2014 `LightConeBasis.relativeTransverse (L) (k P : V) := L.transverseProj k - (L.plus k / L.plus P) \u2022 L.transverseProj P`, with the membership and `transverseProj P = 0` lemmas there \u2014 and set `deltaLostRelativeTransverse L K := L.relativeTransverse (deltaLost K) K.p`, noting `Lorentz.Vector.relativeTransverse` as the `Vector 3` counterpart in the docstring. This is the same principle the PR applies to `bilinForm_self_eq_two_mul_plus_mul_minus_add`.",
   "issue": "`deltaLostRelativeTransverse L K = L.transverseProj (deltaLost K) - xiLC L K \u2022 L.transverseProj K.p` is exactly the existing relative-transverse construction `Lorentz.Vector.relativeTransverse k P = transversePart k - (plusComponent k / plusComponent P) \u2022 transversePart P` (LightFront.lean:321), specialized to `k = \u0394`, `P = P`; its lemma `deltaLostRelativeTransverse_eq_transverseProj_deltaLost_of_transverseProj_p_eq_zero` likewise mirrors `relativeTransverse_of_transversePart_eq_zero` (LightFront.lean:354). The repo now carries the same notion twice with no cross-reference, and the new copy is tied to one pair of momenta so TMD/GPD users of the `LightConeBasis` layer will add a third.",
